  "get_workspace_info": {
    "description": "Get current workspace information (name, ID, description, organization).\n\nWHEN TO CALL:\n- User asks \"What workspace am I in?\" or \"Show me workspace info\"\n- Need workspace metadata for display or other operations\n- Verifying workspace access and context\n\nDEFAULT BEHAVIOR:\n- No parameters required - uses current user's workspace context\n- Returns workspace metadata including ID, name, description, organization details\n- Includes current user's access context and hostname/environment information\n\nReturns:\n    Workspace object with workspace metadata.\n\nRaises:\n    DataParsingError: If workspace data cannot be parsed.\n    ServiceError: If service communication fails.\n\nExamples:\n    get_workspace_info()  # Get current workspace information",
    "input_schema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "get_workspace_info"
  },
  "list_workspace_attributes": {
    "description": "List all attributes in the workspace (returns list of attribute objects with IDs and titles).\n\nWHEN TO CALL:\n- Need attribute IDs for filtering, slicing, or other operations\n- User asks \"What attributes are available?\" or \"Show me all dimensions\"\n- Exploring workspace data model structure\n\nDEFAULT BEHAVIOR:\n- Returns all attributes if no filters specified\n- Only shows attributes the current user has access to\n- Supports pagination via limit parameter\n\nReturns:\n    AttributesListResponse with attributes list (each has id, title), count, and message.\n\nRaises:\n    ValidationError: If parameters invalid.\n    ServiceError: If service communication fails.\n\nExamples:\n    list_workspace_attributes()  # All attributes\n    list_workspace_attributes(rsql_filter=\"title=like=*customer*\")  # Search\n    list_workspace_attributes(include=[\"labels\", \"datasets\"])  # With relationships",
    "input_schema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "include": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional related entity types to include. Example: [\"labels\", \"datasets\"]"
        },
        "limit": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional maximum attributes to return. Recommended: 10-50 for browsing."
        },
        "rsql_filter": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional RSQL filter. Operators: ==, =in=, =like=, =contains=, =containsic=. Example: title=like=*customer* or id==customer.name"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "list_workspace_attributes"
  },
  "list_workspace_metrics": {
    "description": "List metrics in the workspace with optional relation validation.\n\nWHEN TO CALL:\n- Need metric IDs for create_metric_alert or other operations\n- User asks \"What metrics are available?\" or \"Show me all metrics\"\n- Searching for specific metrics by name\n- Get a single metric by ID: use rsql_filter=\"id==<metric_id>\"\n- Validate metric health: use validate_relations=True\n- NOT for getting full analytics model (use get_workspace_analytics instead)\n\nRELATION VALIDATION (validate_relations=True):\n- Performs runtime validation against the database for all returned metrics\n- Checks if all referenced objects (facts, attributes, metrics in MAQL) exist\n- Each metric's areRelationsValid=true if all references are valid\n- Each metric's areRelationsValid=false if any referenced object is missing\n- Useful for detecting broken metrics after LDM changes or object deletions\n\nDEFAULT BEHAVIOR:\n- Returns all metrics if no filters specified\n- Only shows metrics the current user has access to\n- Supports pagination via limit parameter\n\nReturns:\n    MetricsListResponse with metrics list (each has id, title, maql), count, and message.\n    When validate_relations=True, each metric includes areRelationsValid field.\n    Use metric.id in create_metric_alert.\n\nRaises:\n    ValidationError: If parameters invalid.\n    ServiceError: If service communication fails.\n\nExamples:\n    list_workspace_metrics()  # All metrics\n    list_workspace_metrics(rsql_filter=\"id==revenue\")  # Single metric by ID\n    list_workspace_metrics(rsql_filter=\"id==revenue\", validate_relations=True)  # With validation\n    list_workspace_metrics(rsql_filter=\"title=like=*revenue*\", limit=50)  # Search with pagination\n    list_workspace_metrics(include=[\"facts\", \"attributes\"])  # With relationships",
    "input_schema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "include": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional related entity types to include. Example: [\"facts\", \"attributes\"]"
        },
        "limit": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional maximum metrics to return. Recommended: 10-50 for browsing."
        },
        "rsql_filter": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Optional RSQL filter. Operators: ==, =in=, =like=, =contains=, =containsic=. Use id==<metric_id> to get a single metric. Example: title=like=*revenue* or id==my-metric"
        },
        "validate_relations": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "If True, validates all object references in the metrics (e.g., facts, attributes, other metrics referenced in MAQL). Each metric's areRelationsValid field will be populated: true if all references are valid, false if any referenced object is missing or broken. Use this to check metric health before using them in reports or alerts.",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "list_workspace_metrics"
  }
}
